ISO-10303-21;
/* Tsh249: THREE independent OPEN_SHELLs, each one fin-shaped ADVANCED_FACE radiating from the X-axis (y=0,z=0) in a distinct angular half-plane, each contributing a free boundary edge that is a DIFFERENT overlapping sub-segment of that one line: fin_a x:[0,6], fin_b x:[2,8] (overlaps fin_a in x:[2,6]), fin_c x:[4,10] (overlaps fin_b in x:[4,8], and overlaps fin_a directly in x:[4,6]) — a genuine 3-section fragment chain requiring transitive cutting-node adjacency discovery to fold into one non-manifold edge, purpose-built distinct from Sw001's single shared EDGE_LOOP (only 2 distinct sections) and M045's incidental single-point T-junction (unproven chain) */
